# 1. Introduction

The \textbf{S}tandard \textbf{P}ackage \textbf{L}ibrary (\texttt{SPL}) is a collection of reusable software components that are intended to be used in the development of scientific applications. The \texttt{SPL} library is organized into packages, each of which contains a set of related components. The \texttt{SPL} library is designed to be used with the \texttt{SciPy} library, which is a collection of scientific computing tools for Python.

The \texttt{SPL} library is available at \url{https://github.com/scipy/spl}. It is currently under development, and we welcome contributions from the community.

\section{The \texttt{SPL} library}

The \texttt{SPL} library is divided into several packages, each of which is described below.

\subsection{The \texttt{array\_processing} package}

The \texttt{array\_processing} package contains functions for processing arrays. These include functions for filtering, sorting, and reshaping arrays.

